  "issue": "Lexer Error in CSharpLexer with Keyword Recognition\n\nI've encountered an issue with the CSharpLexer in the Pygments library where certain C# keywords are not being recognized correctly, leading to a lexer error. This seems to be related to recent changes in the keyword list and regex patterns.\n\n### Description\n\nAfter updating the lexer, I noticed that some C# keywords, particularly those related to contextual keywords and class modifiers, are not being parsed as expected. This results in an error during the lexing process, which interrupts the normal flow of the application.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Use the CSharpLexer to parse a C# file containing various keywords, including contextual keywords like `record`, `init`, and `with`.\n2. Observe the lexer output or any errors that occur during the lexing process.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe lexer should correctly identify and parse all C# keywords, including contextual ones, without errors.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nThe lexer fails to recognize certain keywords, resulting in an error that halts the lexing process.\n\n### Additional Information\n\n- The issue seems to be related to the recent changes in the keyword list and regex patterns in the lexer.\n- The error occurs during the collection phase of the test suite, indicating a problem with keyword recognition.\n\nAny insights or suggestions on how to address this issue would be greatly appreciated.",
